  "scope": "Original1ED0 ID scan, argument construction, real MSVCRT sscanf, zero-buffer/name copy and1160 underscore normalization execute on all78 decoded source patterns. Each ID stays below native150-record capacity. Actual GetMagicTbl projects both six-value strips, two frame counts, type and sound fields for every matching source magic row. Current JSON raw frame strips/type/sounds match. Six magic rows referencing absent64/65 project zero fields from untouched image slots even after a valid pattern; current missingSource/type0 and adapter inert sound-1 are distinguished from literal native sound0. Source lines/stack/temporary buffer/parsed-magic-record handoff and C-locale TLS/locks are supplied; archive/stdio/outer file loop/DLL initialization, missing-pattern visual dispatch, drawing, audio and elapsed playback speed are not claimed. Runtime type11 count8 override/charge branches are outside this raw-field comparison. Separately, actual UserUnit Magic export and actual setunit lookup prepare144 source/target contexts; both whole736-byte records match explicit slot writes. Missing64/65 and defined no-effect11 still prepare live flags/timers; inactive or disabled caster leaves its record unchanged while target preparation continues. HP0/80 are not caster gates here. This linked UserUnit instance uses the independently parser-validated CSV rows and supplied loaded flag; its pattern slots remain zero because this export only uses the projected radius for slot preparation, not effect-type dispatch. Clock/source records are supplied; later visual Update/type dispatch/clearing/drawing, Unity state integration and frame speed are not checked.",
